valuate as-is (<=4096 iters each); memoise pure static calls | certain (timed) |\n| 98 | Generated look-alike decoy members (unreferenced `seal*`/`mix*` fns and `K*` consts with the same shape) | seen D23 (\"generated false positives\") | only members reachable from `Release.code` matter | several same-signature static long fns, `static final long K<word><hex>` never read | entry-point evaluation, never regex-compose (`ans_compose_scan` returns decoys) | high |\n| 99 | Chain reading Android state (assets JSON `build`, PackageManager signatures, Resources/arsc, SharedPreferences, `Build.*`, `Settings.Secure`) | gap (D23 `Release` stores the Context in a static but never reads it) | value depends on the APK's own bytes/facts via Context APIs | `ctx`/`getAssets`/`getPackageManager`/`getResources`/`JSONObject` in the chain | `analysis-android-api-stubs` prebuild (stubs answer from the APK + clean retail device) | high: why else pass a Context |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23 TT + every Mastery set) -> answer is COMPUTED: step 5a.\n   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    D16 gate Java_*_native*(int)+*_accepts: objdump -d (bypass len 65536)\n                                    D23 v2 d15 set: Java_*_nativeShare(long) called MID-CHAIN, pure arithmetic: port or unicorn\n   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS-\n   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code (D20 plain dex): strings -a first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> known-\n                                    plaintext unwrap; >1 payload -> host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> member the host names\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml / resources.arsc   aapt dump xmltree ... ; aapt dump --values resources x.apk\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23: all v2); decode each APK alone; loop all answer_ids.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts,\ncert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode,\ndalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval,\ndex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly,\ndex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs,\nentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval,\nhermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key,\nil2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse,\njni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify,\nkey-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\nnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\nnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\npayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nroot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\ntiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D23: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc continues one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation); still unnamed: emulator detection, tamper/repackaging/installer/signature, attestation (Play Integrity,\nkey attestation), then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The big change is structural: since D23 the\ntimed builds (TT + every Mastery set, old days included) COMPUTE the answer in dex (`Release.code`), so each new theme\nwill most likely arrive as a gate fn / probe set inside that chain, and soon as real Android API reads through the\nContext it already receives. Priority 1 = a fast, sandbox-safe v2 evaluator (incl. JNI bridge and Context stubs).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: TT/Mastery were hand-solved (jadx + javac) while the generalize workers were cut off at CORRECT, so solve.py kept no v2 path and tomorrow's Mastery (which mixes old days, now regenerated as v2) would be silent again. Harness note: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish (offline, no clock) and require a passing `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json (D23 variant cases have expected {}).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-release-code-eval\", \"concept\": \"puzzle v2 `analysis`: evaluate the answer-producing method (`Release.code(Context)`) in pure python (rows 69, 96, 97, 98)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT + all 7 Mastery sets shipped `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.mobile.puzzle.v2\\\",\\\"codec\\\":\\\"analysis\\\",\\\"build\\\":..}` with no data; the carried-over solver was silent and `bytecode_vm_scan`/_DxVM resolved only 2 of 8 APKs. Build `analysis_scan(apk)` and call it from extract_answer/puzzle_candidates when the puzzle has no `data` or codec == analysis: (1) locate the entry: the method whose String result ChallengeActivity appends before `&proof=` (fallback: any static `(Landroid/content/Context;)Ljava/lang/String;` on a class named Release, then any static method returning a String that starts with const `ANS-`); (2) run it in the lib Dalvik evaluator with a stub Context object (sput-object to a static must work), executing <clinit> of every touched class first (K consts may be computed, not const-wide), full long ALU (add/sub/mul/xor/or/and/shl/shr/ushr-long incl. /2addr and lit forms, int<->long conversions, cmp-long), new-array/aget-wide/aput-wide/fill-array-data, StringBuilder.append(String|char), String.charAt, Long.toHexString, loops of up to ~4096*N iterations (Probe.s1/s2/s3 inverse searches) with a step budget >= 5M and wall clock <0.8 s per APK; (3) also evaluate `Release.proof` and report consistency (proof == Long.toHexString(token)). Return only the value produced by the entry, never regex-composed candidates. Regression fixtures: the 8 v2 APKs under challenges/day23/mobile-hook-line-and-signal (TT + mastery attempt 1d39aa76, set5 needs the native bridge).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-native-bridge\", \"concept\": \"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-android-api-stubs\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain reads Android state through the Context it is handed: answer from the APK's own bytes + a clean retail device (row 99)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 `Release.code(Context)` stores ctx in a static but never reads it -- a loaded gun for the next days (emulator/tamper/attestation themes). Give the evaluator Context stubs that answer from the APK itself: getAssets().open(name) -> zip entry bytes (InputStream read/readAllBytes/available), org.json JSONObject(String).getString/getInt/getLong/optString (so `build`/`day` fields can seed the chain), getResources().getString(id)/getIdentifier via resources.arsc (resource-id-const-resolve built), getPackageName() -> manifest package, getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES) -> real cert bytes (signing_certs), versionCode/versionName/firstInstallTime constants, getApplicationInfo().flags from the manifest (debuggable bit), getSharedPreferences -> empty with defaults returned, Build.FINGERPRINT/MODEL/MANUFACTURER/BRAND/HARDWARE/TAGS/TYPE -> a retail Pixel (release-keys, user), Settings.Secure ANDROID_ID -> fixed 16 hex, System.getProperty -> JVM-like defaults, SystemClock/nanoTime monotonic small deltas. Plug in the existing clean_device_scan probe tables (emulator/hook/root/installer) so a probe inside the chain gets the clean answer. Log every stub hit for the worker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-pure-static-memo\", \"concept\": \"keep a pure-python Dalvik evaluation of a v2 chain under the timed budget for 7+ sets (rows 96, 97)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Mastery grew to 7 sets (D23) and each solve must stay <1 s total. v2 chains call Probe.s1/s2/s3 (up to 4096 iterations of ~10 ops) 3-6 times per set plus table walks. Add: memoisation of static methods whose bodies touch no static fields/arrays/invokes outside the pure set (key = method + args); a recognizer that turns `i=0; while(f(i)!=t){i++; if(i>=N) return -1}` into a direct python loop over a compiled lambda of f; precompiled per-method python closures (translate the straight-line long-ALU basic blocks once, then run); per-set fork already exists in solverrt. Target: all 8 day23 v2 APKs < 0.3 s each on the Homebase VM.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"play-integrity-verdict-select\", \"concept\": \"Play Integrity / SafetyNet verdict JSON drives the branch: pick the value for the strongest clean verdict (row 87)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"attestation-jws-claims (built) decodes tokens. Add verdict semantics: parse decoded payloads or plain JSON assets with requestDetails{requestPackageName, nonce, timestampMillis}, appIntegrity{appRecognitionVerdict PLAY_RECOGNIZED|UNRECOGNIZED_VERSION|UNEVALUATED, packageName, certificateSha256Digest[], versionCode}, deviceIntegrity{deviceRecognitionVerdict [MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY, MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY, MEETS_STRONG_INTEGRITY, MEETS_VIRTUAL_INTEGRITY]}, accountDetails{appLicensingVerdict LICENSED}, legacy SafetyNet ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity/evaluationType HARDWARE_BACKED. When several verdict blobs or dex branches exist, rank the one with PLAY_RECOGNIZED + MEETS_DEVICE/STRONG_INTEGRITY + LICENSED + certificateSha256Digest equal to signing_certs(apk) + nonce matching the host's computed nonce; report the ANS- value tied to it; demote others as decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"entry-anchored-candidate-veto\", \"concept\": \"reject ANS-shaped candidates that the entry method does not produce: hex-table and dead-mixer decoys (row 98)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 v2 dex holds `ANS-` and `0123456789ABCDEF` consts in Release plus unreferenced look-alike mixers (`sealTrampolinec7`, `sealHook30`, `K*` longs); `ans_compose_scan` returned several ANS-shaped DECOYS and a naive compose gives `ANS-0123456789ABCDEF` (also the harness placeholder). In extract_answer's ranking: when an entry-evaluated value exists (analysis_scan/proof_flow_scan), drop every other code-side candidate; never emit a candidate equal to the hex alphabet; demote candidates from methods unreachable from ChallengeActivity/MainActivity (entry-reachable-callgraph-rank built) and from fns whose only callers are themselves dead. Unit test on the day23 TT APK: only ANS-E4F679E90A7D1CAE-shaped output from Release.code survives.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-long-intrinsics\", \"concept\": \"java.lang / kotlin intrinsics a mixer chain may call (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 mixers inline rotates as shl/ushr pairs; the next generator may call the library: Long.rotateLeft/rotateRight/reverse/reverseBytes/bitCount/numberOfLeadingZeros/numberOfTrailingZeros/highestOneBit/signum, Long.divideUnsigned/remainderUnsigned/compareUnsigned/toUnsignedString/parseUnsignedLong/parseLong(s,16)/toString(v,36), Integer.* equivalents, Math.floorMod/floorDiv/abs/multiplyHigh/multiplyExact (raise on overflow), Math.multiplyHigh/unsignedMultiplyHigh, String.format(\\\"%016X\\\"|\\\"%016x\\\"|\\\"%08X\\\", ..) and Locale variants, Long.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode, CRC32/Adler32 update/getValue, MessageDigest SHA-256/MD5 over byte[] (+ BigInteger(1,d).toString(16)), kotlin ULong ops (`ULong.constructor-impl`, `UnsignedKt.ulongRemainder`, `Long.rotateLeft` in kotlin.Bits). Implement in the evaluator's intrinsic table with exact Java semantics (two's complement wrap, sign extension).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-object-chain-eval\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain written in Kotlin: `object` singletons, companion objects, @JvmStatic, top-level `*Kt` classes, inline classes (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D23 chain is plain static Java. A Kotlin build would compile Mix.f1 to `Mix.INSTANCE.f1(j)` (sget-object INSTANCE + invoke-virtual/final), companion `Release.Companion.code(ctx)`, top-level fns in `ReleaseKt`, `Intrinsics.checkNotNullParameter` calls, `ULong` boxing (`ULong.box-impl`), lambdas (`$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0`, invoke-custom), `when` -> sparse-switch. Make the evaluator: run <clinit> to build INSTANCE/Companion, dispatch invoke-virtual on singleton receivers by class, treat kotlin.jvm.internal.Intrinsics.* as no-ops, unbox inline classes, follow synthetic accessor `access$`. Test with a tiny hand-built dex (dexlib-free: reuse the lib's dex writer fixture if present, else skip with a TODO).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"instrumentation-false-positive-env\", \"concept\": \"hook/instrumentation detection where generated benign signals must evaluate as false positives: realistic clean process introspection (rows 48, 91)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 prompt 'Separate real instrumentation signals from generated false positives' shipped only arithmetic, but a real version scores signals: /proc/self/maps lines (libart, libc, libandroid_runtime, app base.apk, `[anon:dalvik-...]`, a benign `libfrida_like_name` or `gadget` substring in an unrelated path), Thread.getAllStackTraces / Throwable stack frames (com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit, RuntimeInit, android.app.ActivityThread -- no de.robv.android.xposed / com.saurik.substrate), /proc/self/task/*/comm names (main, RenderThread, FinalizerDaemon, HeapTaskDaemon -- no gum-js-loop/gmain/pool-frida), open ports (/proc/net/tcp without 27042/27043), Modifier.isNative on the app's own methods (only declared natives), ClassLoader.loadClass('de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge') -> ClassNotFoundException, Debug.isDebuggerConnected false, installed packages without frida/xposed/lsposed managers. Extend hook-framework-introspection-stubs (built) so each probe returns this realistic clean text (with deliberate near-miss substrings) and the app's own filter logic decides; report per-signal verdicts so the worker can see which ones were 'false positives'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening\", \"concept\": \"v2 mixers behind flattening / opaque predicates / string-switch dispatch / reflection (rows 72, 77, 79, 81, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The resilience arc (D17 renaming, D18 strings, D19 reflection, D21 state machine) can now be applied to the v2 chain itself: token() split into a `while(true){switch(state)}` dispatcher, mixers invoked via Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with xor'd names, opaque predicates guarding a decoy mixer, a tiny bytecode VM running the mix. Wire flattened-cfg-switch-eval, reflection-name-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch and tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret (all built) into analysis_scan's evaluator (reflection: resolve Method objects to dex methods and invoke them; Method.invoke boxing/unboxing of Long), with the same <0.8 s budget. Synthetic test: the D23 TT chain rewritten with each transform.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bb7f3122-8fec-42c3-9b8b-efd25a97856c","uuid":"55d25aeb-03fa-47c6-a5ac-51db94fe9e81","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:21:53.249Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| 48 | Emulator / Frida / Xposed detection | partly D23 (hook theme as a pure gate fn; no probe API) | same, gated | `goldfish`, `ranchu`, `ro.kernel.qemu`, `frida`, `27042`, `XposedBridge`, `/proc/self/maps` | `strings -a`; frida [M] | med-high |\n| 91 | Hook-framework detection (Frida, Xposed, Substrate, LSPosed) via introspection | seen D23 (TT/Mastery: theme gate `HookLineAndSignal.instrumentationSignals(a,b,c)=(a^b^c)&7` over `Probe` results inside the v2 chain; no real Frida/Xposed API yet) | value on the \"no hook\" path | `Thread.getStackTrace`/`Throwable.getStackTrace` class names, `/proc/self/task/*/comm` (`gum-js-loop`, `gmain`), `Modifier.isNative` on own methods, `de.robv.android.xposed` | `jadx`; `hook-framework-introspection-stubs` prebuild | high (mixed Mastery); real introspection API still unseen |\n| 93 | Hardware key attestation `RootOfTrust` (cert chain extension OID 1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17: verifiedBootKey, deviceLocked, verifiedBootState, verifiedBootHash, attestationChallenge) | gap (D22 title pun) | a field of the KeyDescription in a shipped DER/PEM cert, or the branch the app takes on `Verified`/`deviceLocked=true` | `getCertificateChain`, `KeyGenParameterSpec.setAttestationChallenge`, `1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17`, `res/raw/*.der\\|*.pem`, `-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE` | `openssl x509 -in c.der -inform DER -text` [i]; `openssl asn1parse` [i]; `key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse` prebuild | high: title pun + Mastery repeats D22 |\n| 94 | Multi-signal root score / per-signal key (each probe contributes a bit, weight or fragment; forcing the aggregate `isRooted()=false` yields a decoy) | gap (D22 prompt \"multiple signals ... without globally patching success\") | value built from the clean result of EVERY signal (bitmask -> key, fragment concat, score threshold) | several probe methods feeding `or-int`/`shl-int`/`add-int` into one int, `StringBuilder.append` per probe, a `success`/`isRooted` field next to the vector | `root-signal-vector-key` prebuild; `clean_device_scan` [i] per probe | high |\n| 95 | Shell / process probes (`Runtime.exec(\"which su\")`, `ProcessBuilder(\"getprop\")`, `mount`, `getenforce`, `id`) | gap | the branch on the process output being empty / `Enforcing` / `ro` | `Ljava/lang/Runtime;->exec`, `ProcessBuilder`, `getInputStream`, `BufferedReader.readLine`, `/proc/mounts`, `/proc/self/mountinfo` | `process-exec-shell-probe-stubs` prebuild | med-high |\n| 92 | Biometric / local authentication bypass (MASVS-AUTH) | gap | `onAuthenticationSucceeded` body (CryptoObject null-tolerant) | `BiometricPrompt$AuthenticationCallback`, `FingerprintManager`, `KeyguardManager.isDeviceSecure`, `setUserAuthenticationRequired` | `jadx`; `biometric-auth-callback-eval` prebuild | med |\n| 96 | Puzzle v2 `analysis`: answer computed by a static 64-bit mixer chain (`Release.code(Context)`) | seen D23 (TT + all Mastery sets) | `Release.code` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 nibbles of `fin(Mix.f1(token())) ^ K`; `token()` = 3 nested static long fns from a `const-wide` seed; `proof()` = `Long.toHexString(token())` gates ChallengeActivity | puzzle `schema ...v2`, `codec:\"analysis\"`, `build`, no `data`; dex 5.3-6.2 KB; classes `Release`/`Probe`/`Mix`/`Util`/`Core`/`Guard`/`Tab`; `0123456789ABCDEF` const | manual: `jadx -q -d j x.apk` + javac with a 1-line `android.content.Context` stub + `Main` printing `Release.code(null)`; timed: pure-python Dalvik eval of `Release.code` (`analysis-release-code-eval` prebuild); `bytecode_vm_scan` [i] partial (2/8) | certain (timed); single may follow |\n| 97 | Probe inverse-search gates (`Probe.s1/s2/s3(a,b,c,d)`: smallest i<4096 with f(i)==d else -1) + theme gate fn over their results | seen D23 | ints folded into the chain via `* K` and xor | `while(((i^c)*a+b)&4095 != d) i++`, rotate-by-`(a%11)+1` variant, `gate*`/`instrumentationSignals` `(x^y^z)&7`/`&255` | evaluate as-is (<=4096 iters each); memoise pure static calls | certain (timed) |\n| 98 | Generated look-alike decoy members (unreferenced `seal*`/`mix*` fns and `K*` consts with the same shape) | seen D23 (\"generated false positives\") | only members reachable from `Release.code` matter | several same-signature static long fns, `static final long K<word><hex>` never read | entry-point evaluation, never regex-compose (`ans_compose_scan` returns decoys) | high |\n| 99 | Chain reading Android state (assets JSON `build`, PackageManager signatures, Resources/arsc, SharedPreferences, `Build.*`, `Settings.Secure`) | gap (D23 `Release` stores the Context in a static but never reads it) | value depends on the APK's own bytes/facts via Context APIs | `ctx`/`getAssets`/`getPackageManager`/`getResources`/`JSONObject` in the chain | `analysis-android-api-stubs` prebuild (stubs answer from the APK + clean retail device) | high: why else pass a Context |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\n0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23 TT + every Mastery set) -> answer is COMPUTED: step 5a.\n   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n                                    D16 gate Java_*_native*(int)+*_accepts: objdump -d (bypass len 65536)\n                                    D23 v2 d15 set: Java_*_nativeShare(long) called MID-CHAIN, pure arithmetic: port or unicorn\n   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS-\n   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code (D20 plain dex): strings -a first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> known-\n                                    plaintext unwrap; >1 payload -> host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> member the host names\n   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n   res/xml/network_security_config.xml / resources.arsc   aapt dump xmltree ... ; aapt dump --values resources x.apk\n   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23: all v2); decode each APK alone; loop all answer_ids.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path, apk-signing-block-payload,\nasset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims, binder-ontransact-code-map,\nbiometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool, cert-and-signing-facts,\ncert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs, custom-alphabet-decode,\ndalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel, decrypt-call-site-args-eval,\ndex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args, dex-native-split-assembly,\ndex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs,\nentry-reachable-callgraph-rank, enum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval,\nhermes-hbc-string-table, hook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key,\nil2cpp-metadata-literals, installer-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, integrity-derived-key, java-serialized-object-parse,\njni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback, jwt-token-decode-verify,\nkey-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures, kotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines,\nmessagedigest-derived-answer, module-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse,\nnative-gated-branch-read, native-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate,\nnative-payload-system-load, native-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs,\nnested-container-recurse, opaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select,\npayload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap, permutation-transposition-family, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nroot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\ntiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\nForecast after D23: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc continues one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation); still unnamed: emulator detection, tamper/repackaging/installer/signature, attestation (Play Integrity,\nkey attestation), then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The big change is structural: since D23 the\ntimed builds (TT + every Mastery set, old days included) COMPUTE the answer in dex (`Release.code`), so each new theme\nwill most likely arrive as a gate fn / probe set inside that chain, and soon as real Android API reads through the\nContext it already receives. Priority 1 = a fast, sandbox-safe v2 evaluator (incl. JNI bridge and Context stubs).\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: TT/Mastery were hand-solved (jadx + javac) while the generalize workers were cut off at CORRECT, so solve.py kept no v2 path and tomorrow's Mastery (which mixes old days, now regenerated as v2) would be silent again. Harness note: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish (offline, no clock) and require a passing `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json (D23 variant cases have expected {}).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-release-code-eval\", \"concept\": \"puzzle v2 `analysis`: evaluate the answer-producing method (`Release.code(Context)`) in pure python (rows 69, 96, 97, 98)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 TT + all 7 Mastery sets shipped `{\\\"schema\\\":\\\"huntress.mobile.puzzle.v2\\\",\\\"codec\\\":\\\"analysis\\\",\\\"build\\\":..}` with no data; the carried-over solver was silent and `bytecode_vm_scan`/_DxVM resolved only 2 of 8 APKs. Build `analysis_scan(apk)` and call it from extract_answer/puzzle_candidates when the puzzle has no `data` or codec == analysis: (1) locate the entry: the method whose String result ChallengeActivity appends before `&proof=` (fallback: any static `(Landroid/content/Context;)Ljava/lang/String;` on a class named Release, then any static method returning a String that starts with const `ANS-`); (2) run it in the lib Dalvik evaluator with a stub Context object (sput-object to a static must work), executing <clinit> of every touched class first (K consts may be computed, not const-wide), full long ALU (add/sub/mul/xor/or/and/shl/shr/ushr-long incl. /2addr and lit forms, int<->long conversions, cmp-long), new-array/aget-wide/aput-wide/fill-array-data, StringBuilder.append(String|char), String.charAt, Long.toHexString, loops of up to ~4096*N iterations (Probe.s1/s2/s3 inverse searches) with a step budget >= 5M and wall clock <0.8 s per APK; (3) also evaluate `Release.proof` and report consistency (proof == Long.toHexString(token)). Return only the value produced by the entry, never regex-composed candidates. Regression fixtures: the 8 v2 APKs under challenges/day23/mobile-hook-line-and-signal (TT + mastery attempt 1d39aa76, set5 needs the native bridge).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-native-bridge\", \"concept\": \"Dalvik evaluator calls a `native` method mid-chain by emulating its `Java_*` export (rows 37, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 Mastery d15 set: `NativeLibrarySecrets.nativeShare(long)` (static native, `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` in <clinit>) sits inside Release.token(); `lib/x86_64/libarena.so` (13512 B) exports `Java_<pkg>_NativeLibrarySecrets_nativeShare` = ~10 insns of movabs/add/xor/imul/rol on rdx. The LLM worker used ctypes.CDLL on the host (sandbox violation). In the evaluator: when invoke-static/virtual hits a method with ACC_NATIVE, mangle the JNI name (incl. overloaded `__<sig>` form and `_1`/`_0xxxx` escapes), find the export in lib/<abi>/*.so (x86_64 first, then arm64-v8a/armeabi-v7a/x86), and run it under unicorn (reuse native-so-emulate-export): JNIEnv* -> a fake function table whose slots return 0/trap, jclass/jobject = dummy handles, long/int args per SysV (rdx, rcx, r8...) or AAPCS64 (x2, x3...), return rax/x0 masked to the declared type; jstring returns via a NewStringUTF stub that records the C string. Budget 200k insns. Also support RegisterNatives tables (registernatives-table built). Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-android-api-stubs\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain reads Android state through the Context it is handed: answer from the APK's own bytes + a clean retail device (row 99)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 `Release.code(Context)` stores ctx in a static but never reads it -- a loaded gun for the next days (emulator/tamper/attestation themes). Give the evaluator Context stubs that answer from the APK itself: getAssets().open(name) -> zip entry bytes (InputStream read/readAllBytes/available), org.json JSONObject(String).getString/getInt/getLong/optString (so `build`/`day` fields can seed the chain), getResources().getString(id)/getIdentifier via resources.arsc (resource-id-const-resolve built), getPackageName() -> manifest package, getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES) -> real cert bytes (signing_certs), versionCode/versionName/firstInstallTime constants, getApplicationInfo().flags from the manifest (debuggable bit), getSharedPreferences -> empty with defaults returned, Build.FINGERPRINT/MODEL/MANUFACTURER/BRAND/HARDWARE/TAGS/TYPE -> a retail Pixel (release-keys, user), Settings.Secure ANDROID_ID -> fixed 16 hex, System.getProperty -> JVM-like defaults, SystemClock/nanoTime monotonic small deltas. Plug in the existing clean_device_scan probe tables (emulator/hook/root/installer) so a probe inside the chain gets the clean answer. Log every stub hit for the worker.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-pure-static-memo\", \"concept\": \"keep a pure-python Dalvik evaluation of a v2 chain under the timed budget for 7+ sets (rows 96, 97)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Mastery grew to 7 sets (D23) and each solve must stay <1 s total. v2 chains call Probe.s1/s2/s3 (up to 4096 iterations of ~10 ops) 3-6 times per set plus table walks. Add: memoisation of static methods whose bodies touch no static fields/arrays/invokes outside the pure set (key = method + args); a recognizer that turns `i=0; while(f(i)!=t){i++; if(i>=N) return -1}` into a direct python loop over a compiled lambda of f; precompiled per-method python closures (translate the straight-line long-ALU basic blocks once, then run); per-set fork already exists in solverrt. Target: all 8 day23 v2 APKs < 0.3 s each on the Homebase VM.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"play-integrity-verdict-select\", \"concept\": \"Play Integrity / SafetyNet verdict JSON drives the branch: pick the value for the strongest clean verdict (row 87)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"attestation-jws-claims (built) decodes tokens. Add verdict semantics: parse decoded payloads or plain JSON assets with requestDetails{requestPackageName, nonce, timestampMillis}, appIntegrity{appRecognitionVerdict PLAY_RECOGNIZED|UNRECOGNIZED_VERSION|UNEVALUATED, packageName, certificateSha256Digest[], versionCode}, deviceIntegrity{deviceRecognitionVerdict [MEETS_BASIC_INTEGRITY, MEETS_DEVICE_INTEGRITY, MEETS_STRONG_INTEGRITY, MEETS_VIRTUAL_INTEGRITY]}, accountDetails{appLicensingVerdict LICENSED}, legacy SafetyNet ctsProfileMatch/basicIntegrity/evaluationType HARDWARE_BACKED. When several verdict blobs or dex branches exist, rank the one with PLAY_RECOGNIZED + MEETS_DEVICE/STRONG_INTEGRITY + LICENSED + certificateSha256Digest equal to signing_certs(apk) + nonce matching the host's computed nonce; report the ANS- value tied to it; demote others as decoys.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"entry-anchored-candidate-veto\", \"concept\": \"reject ANS-shaped candidates that the entry method does not produce: hex-table and dead-mixer decoys (row 98)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 v2 dex holds `ANS-` and `0123456789ABCDEF` consts in Release plus unreferenced look-alike mixers (`sealTrampolinec7`, `sealHook30`, `K*` longs); `ans_compose_scan` returned several ANS-shaped DECOYS and a naive compose gives `ANS-0123456789ABCDEF` (also the harness placeholder). In extract_answer's ranking: when an entry-evaluated value exists (analysis_scan/proof_flow_scan), drop every other code-side candidate; never emit a candidate equal to the hex alphabet; demote candidates from methods unreachable from ChallengeActivity/MainActivity (entry-reachable-callgraph-rank built) and from fns whose only callers are themselves dead. Unit test on the day23 TT APK: only ANS-E4F679E90A7D1CAE-shaped output from Release.code survives.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-long-intrinsics\", \"concept\": \"java.lang / kotlin intrinsics a mixer chain may call (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 mixers inline rotates as shl/ushr pairs; the next generator may call the library: Long.rotateLeft/rotateRight/reverse/reverseBytes/bitCount/numberOfLeadingZeros/numberOfTrailingZeros/highestOneBit/signum, Long.divideUnsigned/remainderUnsigned/compareUnsigned/toUnsignedString/parseUnsignedLong/parseLong(s,16)/toString(v,36), Integer.* equivalents, Math.floorMod/floorDiv/abs/multiplyHigh/multiplyExact (raise on overflow), Math.multiplyHigh/unsignedMultiplyHigh, String.format(\\\"%016X\\\"|\\\"%016x\\\"|\\\"%08X\\\", ..) and Locale variants, Long.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode, CRC32/Adler32 update/getValue, MessageDigest SHA-256/MD5 over byte[] (+ BigInteger(1,d).toString(16)), kotlin ULong ops (`ULong.constructor-impl`, `UnsignedKt.ulongRemainder`, `Long.rotateLeft` in kotlin.Bits). Implement in the evaluator's intrinsic table with exact Java semantics (two's complement wrap, sign extension).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"kotlin-object-chain-eval\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain written in Kotlin: `object` singletons, companion objects, @JvmStatic, top-level `*Kt` classes, inline classes (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The D23 chain is plain static Java. A Kotlin build would compile Mix.f1 to `Mix.INSTANCE.f1(j)` (sget-object INSTANCE + invoke-virtual/final), companion `Release.Companion.code(ctx)`, top-level fns in `ReleaseKt`, `Intrinsics.checkNotNullParameter` calls, `ULong` boxing (`ULong.box-impl`), lambdas (`$$ExternalSyntheticLambda0`, invoke-custom), `when` -> sparse-switch. Make the evaluator: run <clinit> to build INSTANCE/Companion, dispatch invoke-virtual on singleton receivers by class, treat kotlin.jvm.internal.Intrinsics.* as no-ops, unbox inline classes, follow synthetic accessor `access$`. Test with a tiny hand-built dex (dexlib-free: reuse the lib's dex writer fixture if present, else skip with a TODO).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"instrumentation-false-positive-env\", \"concept\": \"hook/instrumentation detection where generated benign signals must evaluate as false positives: realistic clean process introspection (rows 48, 91)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D23 prompt 'Separate real instrumentation signals from generated false positives' shipped only arithmetic, but a real version scores signals: /proc/self/maps lines (libart, libc, libandroid_runtime, app base.apk, `[anon:dalvik-...]`, a benign `libfrida_like_name` or `gadget` substring in an unrelated path), Thread.getAllStackTraces / Throwable stack frames (com.android.internal.os.ZygoteInit, RuntimeInit, android.app.ActivityThread -- no de.robv.android.xposed / com.saurik.substrate), /proc/self/task/*/comm names (main, RenderThread, FinalizerDaemon, HeapTaskDaemon -- no gum-js-loop/gmain/pool-frida), open ports (/proc/net/tcp without 27042/27043), Modifier.isNative on the app's own methods (only declared natives), ClassLoader.loadClass('de.robv.android.xposed.XposedBridge') -> ClassNotFoundException, Debug.isDebuggerConnected false, installed packages without frida/xposed/lsposed managers. Extend hook-framework-introspection-stubs (built) so each probe returns this realistic clean text (with deliberate near-miss substrings) and the app's own filter logic decides; report per-signal verdicts so the worker can see which ones were 'false positives'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening\", \"concept\": \"v2 mixers behind flattening / opaque predicates / string-switch dispatch / reflection (rows 72, 77, 79, 81, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The resilience arc (D17 renaming, D18 strings, D19 reflection, D21 state machine) can now be applied to the v2 chain itself: token() split into a `while(true){switch(state)}` dispatcher, mixers invoked via Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod with xor'd names, opaque predicates guarding a decoy mixer, a tiny bytecode VM running the mix. Wire flattened-cfg-switch-eval, reflection-name-resolve, opaque-predicate-dead-branch and tiny-bytecode-vm-interpret (all built) into analysis_scan's evaluator (reflection: resolve Method objects to dex methods and invoke them; Method.invoke boxing/unboxing of Long), with the same <0.8 s budget. Synthetic test: the D23 TT chain rewritten with each transform.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DCjUgtynXe7d9ThKD9ouyT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
