{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgM8rhA5foPhZsP7josFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N6CyhRrTvuc68AzTuknaP4","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; grep -n '^| 48 ' reference/coverage/mobile-android.md | cut -c1-400; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index(\"binder-ontransact-code-map,\"); \n# rebuild built list\nst=json.load(open('.run/prebuild-state.json'))\nbuilt=sorted(k.split(':',1)[1] for k,v in st.items() if k.startswith('mobile-android:') and (v.get('ok') or v.get('attempts',0)>=2))\ni=s.index(\"Already built (prebuild-state ok, dropped from the list):\")\nj=s.index(\"```json\", i)\nlines=[]; cur=\"\"\nfor n in built:\n    t=(cur+\" \" if cur else \"\")+n+\",\"\n    if len(t)>118: lines.append(cur); cur=n+\",\"\n    else: cur=t\nlines.append(cur[:-1]+\".\")\nprose = \"Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\"\"\nForecast after D24: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook/\ninstrumentation, D24 emulator) and the v2 chain absorbs each one as a single pure gate fn -- D23 and D24 were the same\ngenerator with new names. Still unnamed (D25-D31, 7 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / APK signature / installer\nsource, self-integrity (dex CRC / checksum), attestation (Play Integrity, key attestation), certificate pinning, then\nobfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box). The next structural step is the chain reading the Context it already\nreceives (signature bytes, zip CRC, Build/props, keystore certs) or doing float/Random math; the D24 prompt's \"pinned\nemulator used by the solve oracle\" means any environment read must be answered as the oracle's stock AVD, not only as a\nclean Pixel. Mastery grows +1 set per day (D24: 8) -- keep the per-set solve far under the window.\n\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:i]+prose+s[j:]\nk=s.index(\"```json\"); e=s.index(\"```\", k+7)\nold=json.loads(s[k+7:e])\nkeep={g['id']:g for g in old}\nnew=[]\nnew.append(keep['worker-cue-inline'])\nnew.append({\"id\":\"pinned-emulator-env-profile\",\"concept\":\"environment probes answered as the solve oracle's PINNED stock emulator, alongside the clean-Pixel profile (rows 48, 99)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 prompt: 'Defeat app-owned environment checks on the same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle' -- the reference answer is produced ON an emulator, so if a chain ever reads the environment, the clean-Pixel stubs (clean-device-env-stubs, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, analysis-android-api-stubs) may give the WRONG value. Add a second env profile to the deep evaluator and to clean_device_scan: a stock Google AVD x86_64 (Build.FINGERPRINT google/sdk_gphone64_x86_64/emu64x:14/...:userdebug/dev-keys, MODEL sdk_gphone64_x86_64, MANUFACTURER Google, BRAND google, HARDWARE ranchu, PRODUCT sdk_gphone64_x86_64, DEVICE emu64x, BOARD goldfish_x86_64, TAGS dev-keys, TYPE userdebug; ro.kernel.qemu=1, ro.boot.qemu=1, ro.hardware=ranchu, qemu.sf.lcd_density, /dev/qemu_pipe + /dev/goldfish_pipe present; TelephonyManager operator 'Android'/'310260', line1 15555215554, deviceId 358240051111110; sensor list with 'Goldfish 3-axis Accelerometer'; battery 50%/AC). Evaluate the entry under BOTH profiles; if the values differ, return both with labels (emulator first when the prompt says 'pinned emulator'/'solve oracle', clean first otherwise) and log which probe diverged. Keep the clean profile the default for v1 code-side scans.\"})\nnew.append({\"id\":\"analysis-self-integrity-stubs\",\"concept\":\"anti-tamper / repackaging inside the v2 chain: signature bytes, signing-cert digest, own dex CRC / checksum folded into the seed (rows 99, 49)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Likeliest next resilience control (D25+). The chain would do: ctx.getPackageManager().getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNATURES|GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signatures[0] -> .hashCode() (= Arrays.hashCode(toByteArray()) Java int semantics) / .toByteArray() -> MessageDigest SHA-256|SHA-1|MD5 -> fold into a long (ByteBuffer.wrap(d).getLong(), or loop `v = v*31 + b`); ctx.getApplicationInfo().sourceDir / getPackageCodePath() -> new ZipFile(path).getEntry(\\\"classes.dex\\\").getCrc() / .getSize(); CRC32/Adler32 over the dex or the puzzle asset; getInstallerPackageName / getInstallSourceInfo -> 'com.android.vending'. Answer every stub from the APK's OWN bytes: signing cert = the PKCS#7 in META-INF/*.RSA|*.DSA|*.EC (v1) or the v2/v3 signing block (signing_certs exists), zip entry CRC/size from the central directory, dex bytes as shipped. Exact Java semantics for Signature.hashCode, String.hashCode, Arrays.hashCode(byte[]), byte sign extension. Test: a synthetic chain over the D24 TT fixture; regression: D23/D24 v2 APKs unchanged.\"})\nnew.append({\"id\":\"dex-eval-float-double-semantics\",\"concept\":\"float/double arithmetic in a v2 chain (sensor readings, scores, thresholds) with exact Java semantics (row 96)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D24 class names already say `SensorMap`/`mixSensor*`; a sensor- or score-based gate would use floats (accelerometer m/s^2, battery temperature, `score > 0.5f`). Make the deep evaluator exact for: add/sub/mul/div/rem-float|double (+2addr), neg-*, int/long<->float/double conversions incl. float-to-int / double-to-long SATURATION and NaN->0, cmpl/cmpg-float|double NaN bias, const/high16 + const-wide/high16 float/double bit patterns, Float.floatToIntBits/floatToRawIntBits/intBitsToFloat, Double.doubleToLongBits/doubleToRawLongBits/longBitsToDouble, Math.round/floor/ceil/sqrt/abs/pow/min/max, StrictMath, Float.compare. Use struct pack/unpack('<f') for float32 rounding after every float op. Unit-test each opcode against known Java outputs.\"})\nnew.append(keep['dex-eval-native-bridge'])\nnew.append({\"id\":\"dex-eval-java-random-lcg\",\"concept\":\"java.util.Random / SplittableRandom / ThreadLocalRandom-free determinism inside the v2 evaluator (row 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"lib already carries the 0x5DEECE66D LCG for v1 scans; the deep evaluator (`_DxeDeepVM`) needs it as intrinsics: new Random(long) (seed ^ 0x5DEECE66D, 48-bit), nextInt(), nextInt(bound) incl. the power-of-two and rejection loop, nextLong(), nextBoolean(), nextDouble() (26+27 bits), nextBytes(byte[]), setSeed; java.util.SplittableRandom(seed).nextLong()/nextInt (mix64 / GOLDEN_GAMMA); Collections.shuffle(list, rnd); UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes (MD5). Unseeded new Random()/Math.random()/System.nanoTime -> report 'non-deterministic' and abort that candidate rather than invent a value.\"})\nnew.append({\"id\":\"analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs\",\"concept\":\"attestation / keystore theme inside the v2 chain: certificate chain bytes and the attestation extension read through KeyStore / CertificateFactory APIs (rows 87, 93)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Attestation is still unnamed in the arc. A v2 version would read a shipped cert: ctx.getResources().openRawResource(R.raw.x) or getAssets().open('attest.der'|'.pem') -> CertificateFactory.getInstance(\\\"X.509\\\").generateCertificate(in) / generateCertificates -> X509Certificate.getExtensionValue(\\\"1.3.6.1.4.1.11129.2.1.17\\\") (OCTET STRING-wrapped DER), getEncoded(), getPublicKey().getEncoded(), getSerialNumber().longValue(), getNotBefore().getTime(), getSubjectX500Principal().getName(); KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").getCertificateChain(alias) -> the shipped chain in order. Implement as evaluator objects backed by the APK's own cert bytes (asn1 via the existing key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse helpers): byte[] results as Python bytearrays with Java signed-byte reads, BigInteger.longValue truncation.\"})\nnew.append({\"id\":\"analysis-interface-signal-list-eval\",\"concept\":\"signals as objects: interface/abstract `Signal` implementations collected in ArrayList/HashMap and iterated, virtual dispatch in the v2 evaluator (rows 94, 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D22-D24 'multiple signals' prompts have so far meant three static Probe calls; the natural next generator step is `List<Check> checks = Arrays.asList(new BoardCheck(), new SensorMap(), ...); for (Check c : checks) score += c.weight() * c.read();`. Support in the deep evaluator: new-instance + <init> + iget/iput (incl. -wide/-object/-boolean), invoke-virtual/-interface dispatch by runtime class (walk superclass chain, default interface methods), java.util.ArrayList/Arrays.asList/List.of/Iterator/for-each, HashMap/LinkedHashMap put/get/entrySet iteration order (insertion for Linked, Java hash order for HashMap -- implement String.hashCode bucket order for small maps), StringBuilder.reverse/insert/setCharAt, String.format('%02x'), Integer.valueOf caching/unboxing. Budget unchanged (<0.3 s per set).\"})\nnew.append({\"id\":\"native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks\",\"concept\":\"JNI export inside the v2 chain that calls back into JNIEnv (strings, static fields, Java methods) (rows 37, 82, 96)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23/D24 d15 set `nativeShare(long)` is pure arithmetic; the next native step uses the env: GetStringUTFChars/ReleaseStringUTFChars on a jstring arg, NewStringUTF result, GetArrayLength/GetByteArrayElements/GetByteArrayRegion on a byte[] arg, FindClass + GetStaticFieldID + GetStaticLongField/GetStaticIntField (read a dex `K*` const), GetStaticMethodID + CallStaticLongMethod(A|V) back into a dex mixer. In solve.py-style unicorn harness (`_native_call`): build a real JNINativeInterface function table (229 slots, each a hook address), resolve each called slot by index, service it from the Dalvik evaluator (strings via a handle table, callbacks re-entering `_DxeDeepVM.run`), then resume. Support x86_64 and